WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.085
Data control is a common reason for local inference.

00:00:03.085 --> 00:00:07.300
Prompts and outputs can remain within an approved environment when the application, logs,

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.300
interfaces, and supporting tools are configured accordingly.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.410
Local execution does not automatically prevent leakage.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.820
Offline capability can support field work, isolated labs, unreliable connectivity,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.070
or continuity needs.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.700
The model, runtime, dependencies, documentation,

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.755
and required reference data must already be available and maintained for offline use to be

00:00:25.755 --> 00:00:26.350
meaningful.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:30.420
Local systems support experimentation with model families, quantizations, prompts,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.800
adapters, and runtimes.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.920
Teams can inspect performance and behavior without every request becoming a metered

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:36.835
external call,

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:40.900
although hardware, electricity, engineering time, and maintenance still have cost.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.945
Customization may include retrieval over approved data, structured workflows,

00:00:44.945 --> 00:00:48.600
domain prompts, fine-tuned or adapted models, and local integrations.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.069
Each change creates evaluation, security, provenance, and lifecycle responsibilities.

00:00:53.069 --> 00:00:57.290
Hosted models may offer stronger capability, larger context, managed scaling,

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.800
rapid updates, and less infrastructure work.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.900
Local models may have lower quality on difficult tasks, limited concurrency,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.800
hardware constraints, and slower access to new capabilities.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.130
Choose local when its control, latency, offline, integration,

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:12.600
or economic benefits match a real requirement.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.615
Do not choose it solely to avoid governance or because hardware ownership feels equivalent

00:01:16.615 --> 00:01:17.400
to privacy.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.200
Hybrid approaches are often practical.
